---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About · b-oss"
  description="About b-oss, the open-source Blipfoto tools project: who started it, and how it is sponsored by Salient Point."
  nav="about"
>
  <Hero label="About hero" icon="b-oss" title="About b-oss">Open source tools for blipfoto.</Hero>

  <section class="block" data-screen-label="About b-oss">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">The project</p>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 18px">
      <p>
        <b>b-oss</b>&nbsp;= Blipfoto - Open Source Software<br />Open source means anyone can
        see the source code, build the software themselves, modify it, and contribute
        improvements back. If you have the skill and the interest, you can join the development
        team.
      </p>
      <p>
        b-oss was started by <strong>Ian Stevenson</strong> — a technologist with thirty years'
        experience as a software engineer and running software companies — using Claude Code and
        other AI tools for implementation. Ian is also one of the directors of blipfoto, but
        b-oss is a personal project and has no formal relationship with blipfoto.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" data-screen-label="Sponsorship">
    <p class="section-eyebrow">Sponsorship</p>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: 18px">
      <p>
        b-oss is sponsored by <a href="https://salientpoint.co.uk">Salient Point</a>, which covers
        certain hosting and development costs, and supports app publication.
      </p>
      <p>
        This relationship is discretionary, and Salient Point does not own the code, apps, data
        or intellectual property for this project. Salient Point has no say over the direction of
        the project, or on authorship or licensing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Layout>
